# Cryptoric Agent — sole maintainer: Itz-Npg <152873138+Itz-Npg@users.noreply.github.com>
#
# There is no team account behind this project and no shared credential of any
# kind. Every key below belongs to the maintainer personally, and every
# contributor is a reader: the signing key, the Apple account, the npm token and
# these provider keys are never shared with a second person. Do not add a
# team-owned address here, and do not put a second person's key in this file —
# it is the one place in the repository where a secret is expected to live, which
# is precisely why nobody else is given access to it.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored and must stay that way.
#
# The main process reads this file once at boot and copies any key it finds
# into the OS-encrypted credential store (safeStorage). The store is what the
# model gateway reads from; a key already in the store wins, and nothing is
# ever written back to this file.

# Hosted models via OpenRouter (https://openrouter.ai/keys).
# Used by the Space Bunny Alpha entry in the model picker.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Hosted models via APINEX (https://apinex.bond/). OpenAI-compatible at
# https://api.apinex.bond/v1. Covers the five free models the provider serves
# on a plain key; the other `free/`-prefixed ids there need a paid subscription.
APINEX_API_KEY=

# Any OpenAI-compatible hosted endpoint, for a key entered in Settings.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mode
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `local` (the default) keeps everything on this machine: coins live in a local
# ledger and nothing but your own model requests leaves the device.
# `hosted` makes the account server the source of truth for identity, coins and
# the model catalogue — so a balance survives uninstalling the app and follows
# you to another device.
#
# Setting one without the other is an error, not a fallback. A build cannot be
# half-hosted: quietly degrading to local would leave you believing your balance
# is synced when it is not.
#
# CRYPTORIC_MODE=local
# AGENT_SERVER_URL=https://api.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Account server (only read when CRYPTORIC_MODE=hosted)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared secret between the app and your account server. Generate with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# AGENT_SERVER_TOKEN=
#
# Plain http is refused on anything that is not loopback, because the account
# token would cross the network in the clear.
# AGENT_SERVER_ALLOW_ORIGIN=
#
# --- server-side, for `agentserver/` ---
# AGENT_SERVER_PORT=8789
#
# MongoDB, so a balance outlives the process. Without it the balance is held in
# memory and a restart resets it. Atlas: set MONGODB_URI plus MONGODB_REGION
# (the Data API is region-scoped). Self-hosted: point MONGODB_URI at an https
# Data API gateway and it is used as-is.
# MONGODB_URI=
# MONGODB_REGION=us-east-1
# MONGODB_DATABASE=cryptoric

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google sign-in
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# An OAuth **client id**, not a secret. Create one in Google Cloud Console with
# type "Desktop app"; the client secret is deliberately unused and must not be
# added here. PKCE means no secret ships with the app, which matters because an
# Electron binary is not a secret store.
#
# A Desktop app client uses a loopback redirect and Google does not match the
# port for it, so registering the URI is not required. If the form does offer an
# "Authorized redirect URIs" field, add exactly this:
#   http://127.0.0.1:53123/callback
#
# Add yourself as a test user on the consent screen as well, or Google answers
# "Access blocked" — an app still in testing mode only admits listed accounts.
#
# Nothing is sent anywhere until this is set. Without it the app says so rather
# than failing at the moment someone presses Sign in.
#
# Verify the handshake for real, with a browser:  npm run test:google
# The console steps, and what each failure means:  docs/google-sign-in.md
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
